# Hand-written, copied by hand out of rocky9-base-conf-validate.log:147 (D14). That
# capture is not vendored: its only record of this shape sits inside a `# record:`
# annotation, and a `#` line is a comment to this tool, so vendoring the file would
# test nothing.
#
# syslog_format was set to 21 names with no `:` among them, which is the
# MAX_SYSLOG_FIELDS cap. The daemon emits every one on the subject side, repeating
# names it has already used, so the record has duplicate keys, no ` : ` separator and
# therefore no object side and no path=. The right answer is a diagnostic, not a
# suggestion. The ANSI bytes in the level prefix are real bytes, not the two-character
# spelling, so strip_ansi is exercised on the way in.
